          "ruleId": "4naly3er__4naly3er_m_centralizationrisk",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "The contract uses a single owner address with unrestricted control over critical administrative functions (transferOwnership, updateBlocklist, updatePenaltyRecipient, unlock, forceUndelegate). There are no multi-signature requirements, timelock delays, or governance mechanisms to distribute control. If the owner key is compromised, an attacker can: 1) Transfer ownership to themselves, 2) Set a malicious blocklist to block arbitrary users, 3) Redirect penalty funds to themselves, 4) Permanently disable the quit lock penalty mechanism via unlock(), 5) Force undelegation of any user's voting power. The comment 'Owner should always be a timelock contract' is not enforced in code.\n\n(no line range: produced by an arm that sends whole files, so nothing bound it to a parsed function)"
