          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "The _checkpoint function contains a for loop that iterates up to 255 times (approximately 5 years of weekly checkpoints) to fill point history. This loop executes on every lock creation, amount increase, time extension, withdrawal, quit, and delegation. As the contract ages, the number of weeks since the last checkpoint grows, causing gas consumption to increase linearly with time. Eventually, the loop will exceed the block gas limit, making all lock management functions unusable and bricking user funds.\n\n(no line range: produced by an arm that sends whole files, so nothing bound it to a parsed function)"
